{
  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_005: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), establishing a weak RNA-only baseline. The central uncertainty is whether the image modality adds any predictive value, which is the core question of a multimodal study. Question tested: config_023 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion) keeps the profile setting and RNA encoder identical to the baseline and introduces only the image encoder and the necessary fusion step. This isolates the contribution of the image modality with minimal confounding. Why best next step: Under a tight budget, directly comparing a multimodal model to the existing RNA-only baseline (same profile, same RNA encoder) gives the cleanest signal on whether adding a second modality is worthwhile. If config_023 substantially exceeds 0.485, we validate the multimodal direction and can then explore encoder/aggregation/fusion variants; if it does not, we learn early that the image modality or simple concat fusion is not the right lever, redirecting effort toward RNA encoder or profile choices. This is more informative than testing image-only (which would not tell us whether fusion works) or jumping to a complex multiprofile multimodal config (which would change too many variables at once)."
}

